+diff --git a/patches/0004-Screenshots-can-no-longer-be-cross-filed-between-cus.patch b/patches/0004-Screenshots-can-no-longer-be-cross-filed-between-cus.patch
+new file mode 100644
+index 0000000..6f86471
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/patches/0004-Screenshots-can-no-longer-be-cross-filed-between-cus.patch
+@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
++From e714da4d43dedf4b57033a5bec7c635d0c9b7ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: max994-dev <bmax994@outlook.com>
++Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:57:51 +0000
++Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Screenshots can no longer be cross-filed between
++ customers; arrests.org forms no longer count as removed when rejected
++MIME-Version: 1.0
++Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
++Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
++
++screenshot_step() named every capture ScreenShot/<date>/<broker>/<HHMMSS>_<step>.png:
++second granularity, no customer in the name. Five workers on the same broker in
++the same second wrote the SAME file and each uploaded it, so one customer's
++filled opt-out form (name, email, home address) was stored as another
++customer's removal evidence and mailed in their quarterly report. 134 customers
++hold such an image; 84 received one in the 1 Oct report; it was still happening
++on 2 Oct. Filenames now carry thread name, microseconds and a random suffix; the
++name-based path in the search helper gets the same treatment.
++
++The shared arrests.org / courtrecords.us template (54 brokers) never filled the
++portal's "Confirm Email" box, so every submission came back "This field is
++required" — and was still returned as a success and marked step=2. 4,093 rows
++across 133 customers were reported as removed without a request ever being
++accepted. The template now fills the confirm field and raises when the portal
