diff --git a/patches/0009-Pace-a-customer-s-removals-across-exactly-one-week.patch b/patches/0009-Pace-a-customer-s-removals-across-exactly-one-week.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b1def18
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/0009-Pace-a-customer-s-removals-across-exactly-one-week.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+From 95ebb7cce081ddf2db7b6c292e32bafa170c175b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: max994-dev <bmax994@outlook.com>
+Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:52:04 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Pace a customer's removals across exactly one week
+
+REMOVAL_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS 1800 -> 0. manage.py treats a non-positive
+value as "derive from the targets": DAYS*86400/TOTAL = 7*86400/413 = 1464s
+(24.4 min), so a customer's full 413-task set spans exactly the 7 days the
+client asked for. The literal 1800 (30 min) stretched the same set to 8.6
+days. Floored at 1s, so this tightens pacing rather than removing it.
+
+Only this line and its explanatory comment differ; every credential in the
+file is byte-identical to the committed version.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+---
+ .env | 6 +++++-
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/.env b/.env
+index 925cef8..c7c7336 100644
+--- a/.env
++++ b/.env
+@@ -10,7 +10,11 @@ DB_SSL_VERIFY_CERT=false
+ # Removal pacing settings
+ REMOVAL_TARGET_DAYS_PER_USER=7
+ REMOVAL_TARGET_TOTAL_PER_USER=413
+-REMOVAL_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1800
++# Client requirement: one customer's removals are spread over ~1 week.
++# 0 = derive the per-user interval as DAYS*86400/TOTAL = 7d/413 tasks
++# = 24.4 min between rows, so the full task set spans exactly 7 days.
++# (Was 1800 = 30 min, which stretched the cycle to 8.6 days.)
++REMOVAL_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS=0
+ 
+ # Upload endpoints
+ SCAN_UPLOAD_URL_TEMPLATE=https://privacyduck.com/scan_api/upload?domain={domain}&user_id={user_id}
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
